# IDX — weekly restore drill. Moved off vanilla cron 2026-08-15 (P2-6): a
# missed Sunday 09:00 fire (laptop asleep/off) was silently skipped for a
# full week with no retry, which is exactly what happened 2026-07-19 to
# 2026-08-15. Persistent=true on the paired .timer fixes that.
#
# Glob is prefix-scoped to walkforward-*.db.zst (P2-6, same date): a bare
# *.db.zst picks the newest backup of EITHER prefix sharing the backup dir,
# so R-5's research.db backup silently made a real drill run verify the
# wrong, tiny, non-critical file while reporting success.
[Unit]
Description=IDX weekly restore drill (verify-only, touches nothing)

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=%h/idx-walkforward-5001
ExecStart=%h/idx-walkforward-5001/scripts/cron_wrap.sh db_restore_drill sh -c 'venv/bin/python3 -m scripts.db_restore "$(ls -t ~/backups/idx-walkforward-5001/walkforward-*.db.zst | head -1)"'
